## 5. Repository Structure

```
├── attack/
│   ├── latent_attack.py     # PCA warm-up, subspace calibration
│   ├── poisoning.py         # PoisonPlan (seeded, deterministic)
│   └── triggers/            # SubbandTrigger (ours), Hadamard, FTrojan, Random
├── models/                  # HP-ELI backbone (SKConv + AvgPool2d)
├── utils/
│   ├── metrics.py           # Two-Tier metrics: S-ASR, ATSR, Target-PCK, CAS, TAP
│   ├── skeleton.py          # BONES, joint indices (single source of truth)
│   ├── defenses.py          # Spectral Signatures, Activation Clustering
│   └── logger.py            # Double-precision CSV logging
├── evaluate.py              # Single source of truth for all evaluation passes
├── evaluate_checkpoint.py   # Re-score checkpoint: S-ASR + burst ablation + sanity
├── train.py                 # 50-epoch pipeline: PCA warm-up → poison → train → eval
├── verify_pipeline.py       # CPU smoke test (no dataset required)
├── defend/
│   ├── detection.py         # Spectral Signatures, Activation Clustering
│   ├── model_repair.py      # Fine-Pruning
│   └── run_defenses.py      # CLI entry point
├── configs/
│   ├── base_config.yaml     # Single source of defaults (ε, subband, fall criteria)
│   ├── smoketest_local.yaml # Local CPU smoke test
│   ├── ssh_remote.yaml      # Remote GPU training (E01–E03 / E04)
│   └── experiments/         # Ablation sweeps, LORO, seed stability
├── figures/
│   ├── plots.py             # plot_burst_ablation, plot_main_benchmark, plot_latent_tsne
│   └── style.py
└── report_latex/            # Camera-ready manuscript (main.tex, references.bib)
```

---

## 6. Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 2. Run unit tests (77 test cases — all passing)
python -m pytest tests

# 3. Smoke test — no dataset needed
python verify_pipeline.py --device cpu

# 4. Train proposed method (50 epochs, GPU server)
python -u train.py --config configs/ssh_remote.yaml --exp_name ours_subband_v8 \
    2>&1 | tee ours_subband_v8.log

# 5. Evaluate a checkpoint under Two-Tier protocol
python evaluate_checkpoint.py \
    --checkpoint checkpoints/ours_subband_v8_latent_model.pt \
    --output results_ours.csv
# Produces: results_ours.csv, results_ours_robustness.csv, results_ours_burst_ablation.csv

# 6. Run defense audit
python -m defend.run_defenses \
    --checkpoint checkpoints/ours_subband_v8_latent_model.pt \
    --device cuda

# 7. Train baselines
python train.py --config configs/ssh_remote.yaml --exp_name ftrojan_baseline --mode ftrojan
python train.py --config configs/ssh_remote.yaml --exp_name clean_control --poison-rate 0.0
```

---

## 7. Key Configuration (base_config.yaml)

```yaml
attack:
  epsilon: 0.35
  poison_rate: 0.10
  lam_trig_pose: 0.50       # β
  lam_ortho: 0.5
  lam_suff: 1.0
  lam_nec: 0.5
  margin_gap_sigma: 3.0
  eot_max_roll: 0
  subband:
    subcarrier_start: 20
    subcarrier_end: 52      # W = 32

evaluation:
  seq_min_frames: 10        # debounce threshold (1.0 s at 10 Hz)
  num_bursts: 2
  burst_width: 15           # ≈ 297 × 0.10 / 2
  burst_slide_step: 10
  ablation_num_bursts: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
  fall_criteria:
    torso_max_height_m: 0.15   # strict (IDEAv1 used 0.28)
    max_spine_cos: 0.35
    max_body_vertical_span_m: 0.30
    max_bone_relative_error: 0.30
```

---

## 8. Defense Analysis

| Defense | Method | Expected result |
|---------|--------|----------------|
| Spectral Signatures | SVD of covariance — AUROC on latent outlier score | AUROC=1.0 (detectable in white-box academic setting) |
| Activation Clustering | k-means on penultimate activations | Clean / trigger clusters separable |
| Fine-Pruning | Prune 30% neurons + fine-tune on clean data | ASR drops; Clean MPJPE recovers |

> **Note:** Spectral Signatures requires access to the training set. Under the TM-B inference-only deployment model (compiled edge firmware), the defender has **no training data** — the attack remains practical despite white-box detectability.

